    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11-0703, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5442\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to the junior\narchery license\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis bill is a necessary amendment to S.177A/A.2021A that passed the\nlegislature earlier this session.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1: Amends paragraph b of subdivision 4 of section(11-0703 of\nthe environmental conservation law as amended by chapter 344 to list\nsomeone who holds a junior archery license as an exception to the\nlanguage in this section that makes someone under 14 ineligible for\nany license.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis is a necessary amendment to S.177A/A.2021A, in order to make\nconforming changes to the section of law referenced above. This will\nensure that there is no conflicting language in statute that could in\nany way hamper the ability of the Department of Environmental\nConservation to implement the intent of the original bill\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nThis is a New Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner\nas a chapter of the laws of 2011, amending the environmental\nconservation law relating to reducing the required minimum age for\nobtaining a junior archery license, as proposed in legislative\nbill numbers S.117-A and A.2021-A, takes effect.\n\n",
